ntdll: a switch to commit the ARM64EC code map whole

FINEWINE_EAGER_CODE_MAP=1 commits the whole map when it is created, as upstream does and as
FineWine did before patch 0035. It costs up to 4 GB in a program that reads through its memory,
so it is only for finding out whether committing the map as it is read is behind a problem.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2801,8 +2801,14 @@
      * reading an untouched page gives the shared zero page. macOS has no such page: every page
      * that is read becomes real memory, and a program that reads through its committed memory
      * (anti-cheat does) pays the whole 4 GB. So it starts out reserved, and a page is committed
-     * the first time something reads it, in virtual_handle_fault. */
-    status = map_view( &arm64ec_view, NULL, size, MEM_TOP_DOWN, VPROT_READ, 0, 0, 0 );
+     * the first time something reads it, in virtual_handle_fault.
+     * FINEWINE_EAGER_CODE_MAP=1 commits it all as upstream does, to rule this in or out when
+     * something misbehaves. */
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "FINEWINE_EAGER_CODE_MAP" );
+        BOOL eager = env && atoi( env );
+        status = map_view( &arm64ec_view, NULL, size, MEM_TOP_DOWN, eager ? VPROT_READ | VPROT_COMMITTED : VPROT_READ, 0, 0, 0 );
+    }
 #else
     status = map_view( &arm64ec_view, NULL, size, MEM_TOP_DOWN, VPROT_READ | VPROT_COMMITTED, 0, 0, 0 );
 #endif
